        "human": "A native Android module used by the Expo project could not be compiled. This is commonly caused by a package version that is incompatible with the current Expo/React Native/Android toolchain.",
        "action": "The Doctor will identify the failing native module and version information, check compatibility signals, and attempt a safe dependency/configuration repair.",
        "confidence": 0.91,
    },
    {
        "name": "Network / package registry failure",
        "patterns": [r"ETIMEDOUT", r"ECONNRESET", r"ENOTFOUND", r"network", r"fetch failed", r"Could not GET"],
        "stage": "Dependency download",
        "human": "The builder could not download a package or Gradle dependency. This is usually a temporary network, registry, or remote-server problem rather than an error in your app.",
        "action": "The Doctor will retry downloads with the configured package manager/Gradle caches before treating the project itself as broken.",
        "confidence": 0.88,
    },
    {
        "name": "APK packaging / validation failure",
